---
title: Sherry Trifle
servings: 6
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Easy
cuisine: British
---

Split the @sponge cakes{1%pack} in half and spread with @strawberry jam{}. Arrange in the bottom of a suitable dish and put a layer of @ratafia biscuits{1%pack} on top. Sprinkle with @sherry{1%wine glass}, two to three wine glasses should be sufficient, do not make it too wet.

Mix the @custard powder{2%tbsp} with a little of the @milk{1%pint} and then add the @sugar{2%tbsp}. Bring the milk to the boil and pour onto the custard mix, stirring all the time. Pour back into the saucepan, or jug if using the microwave, and bring back to the boil to thicken, bearing in mind that the custard will get thicker as it cools.

Pour over the sponge. When cold, place in the fridge.

Top with @double cream{1%pint}{whipped} and decorate just before serving.